{"category":"data-loss","anchor":".claude/scripts/chart-ticket.sh:op_close","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":397,"anchor_line_end":430,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"op_close with --consumed-by skips the interactive-context check (only the --reason branch calls `$DW context`) and never checks the map's Status. chart.md documents the unattended exception as `close <slug> --consumed-by <cycle>` 'on a handed-off map', but the script accepts a `charting` map with open rows, rejects every open ledger row with 'map closed: consumed by ...', closes all its question beads and the epic, and marks the doc closed. Rejection of ledger rows is not reversible by a re-run.","failure_mode":"An autonomous run (or a mistyped slug) that executes `chart-ticket.sh close --map <charting-map> --consumed-by <cycle>` silently destroys the open decision frontier of a map that was never handed off, in exactly the unattended context the feature is meant to forbid.","suggested_fix":"In op_close, when --consumed-by is given require `doc_field Status` == handed-off (or closed, for idempotent re-runs) and refuse otherwise; additionally require that map_rows contains no `open` rows before rejecting anything, mirroring op_handoff's frontier/fog checks.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","answered_by":"claude-headless"}

