### DISS-C-005 [ADVISORY] voice=claude-headless
{"category":"data-loss","anchor":".claude/hooks/safety/block-destructive-bash.sh:_fr11_spike_decided","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":642,"anchor_line_end":657,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"The D-5.9 exception lets `git branch -D spike/<slug>` through when a decided ledger row exists, but a spike branch is defined as 'the pointer for a decision: pushed, never merged'. The function never checks that `refs/remotes/*/spike/<slug>` exists or that the branch has an upstream. The ledger (grimoires/loa/decisions.yaml) is a tracked file the agent can edit with Write, so a row with `status: decided` and `by: operator:x` is cheap to fabricate.","failure_mode":"`git branch -D spike/x` on an unpushed spike with a decided row deletes the only copy of the prototype the spike report's Pointer names; the decision now cites a commit that no longer exists anywhere.","suggested_fix":"In _fr11_spike_decided also require `git rev-parse -q --verify refs/remotes/origin/spike/<slug>` (or any remote-tracking ref for the name) and that the local tip is an ancestor of it; keep the block when either check fails.","anchor_status":"valid","answered_by":"claude-headless"}

### DISS-C-006 [ADVISORY] voice=claude-headless
{"category":"data-loss","anchor":".claude/scripts/chart-ticket.sh:op_epic","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":159,"anchor_line_end":176,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"op_epic's idempotency key is the existence of the map doc. If `br create` succeeds and the doc write fails (mkdir/mktemp/mv error, kill between the two), a re-run finds no doc and runs `br create ... --slug map-<slug>` again, producing two `map` epics. The header promises 're-run ... creates only what is missing', and op_ticket does the bead lookup by external_ref for exactly this reason, but op_epic does not look the epic up by slug/label.","failure_mode":"Duplicate map epics on beads; chart-frontier and op_close only ever address the one the doc names, so the orphan epic stays open forever.","suggested_fix":"Before `br create`, query `beads_all | jq 'select(.issue_type==\"epic\" and (.slug==\"map-<slug>\" or labels contains map and title==...))'` and reuse an existing id; write the doc from the found id.","anchor_status":"valid","answered_by":"claude-headless"}

