{"category":"type-error","anchor":".claude/scripts/beads/get-ready-work.sh:72","anchor_type":"line","anchor_line":72,"anchor_line_end":72,"scope":"cross_file","trigger_anchor":".claude/scripts/chart-frontier.sh:55","cross_file_justification":"chart-frontier.sh (same PR, line 55) matches question beads on `.issue_type // .type`, and the PR's br-stub emits beads the frontier accepts; get-ready-work.sh filters on `.issue_type` alone. The two scripts disagree on the schema inside one PR.","description":"The build-path exclusion that implement.md and implementing-tasks/SKILL.md now rely on (`get-ready-work.sh ... drops question beads`) is `select((.issue_type // \"\") != \"question\")`. A br release or stub that emits `type` instead of `issue_type` passes every question bead through to /implement and /run, while chart-frontier.sh in the same change accepts both keys.","failure_mode":"Decision tickets appear in the build ready set and get claimed/implemented by an autonomous run, which is exactly what create-sprint-task.sh's refusal and the chart.md 'tickets cannot enter a sprint' claim try to prevent.","suggested_fix":"Use `((.issue_type // .type // \"\") | ascii_downcase) != \"question\"` in get-ready-work.sh so both scripts share one predicate; add a bats case with a `type`-only bead.","anchor_status":"valid","answered_by":"claude-headless"}

