### DISS-C-010 [ADVISORY] voice=claude-headless
{"category":"authz","anchor":".claude/scripts/chart-unblock-probe.sh:66","anchor_type":"line","anchor_line":62,"anchor_line_end":76,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"The probe argv runs with the session's full environment and credentials, and the only post-condition is that the main tree's `git status --porcelain` text is unchanged. The throwaway worktree shares `.git` with the main tree, so `git branch -f main HEAD`, `git push`, `git tag`, `git stash`, `git config --global`, and any write outside the repository (~/.ssh, ~/.netrc, /tmp) alter nothing that `git status` reports. Edits to tracked files that were already dirty before the probe are likewise invisible. The skill allowlists this script wholesale, and probe commands can be lifted from untrusted research reports or ticket bodies.","failure_mode":"An unblock ticket probe exfiltrates or mutates state (remote refs, local branches, global git config, home-directory files) while the helper reports 'main tree unchanged' and exit 0.","suggested_fix":"Snapshot and compare `git for-each-ref` and `git stash list` alongside status; run the probe with a minimal env (`env -i PATH=... HOME=<scratch>`), `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null`, and `GIT_DIR` pointing at the worktree only; require the skill to echo the argv to the operator and get confirmation before invoking.","anchor_status":"va

### DISS-C-011 [ADVISORY] voice=claude-headless
{"category":"other","anchor":".claude/scripts/chart-ticket.sh:map_rows","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":143,"anchor_line_end":152,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"map_rows resolves worktree pending ledgers via `${SCRIPT_DIR}/../../grimoires/loa/a2a/*/decisions-pending.yaml` rather than `${ROOT}`, so `--root DIR` (used by the bats fixtures and documented as the fixture tree) still merges the live repo's pending rows into the fixture map. Also, if `dw list` ever prints non-JSON for an empty set, `--argjson a` fails and set -e aborts the command with no message.","failure_mode":"Fixture runs read production pending rows (flaky or wrongly-passing tests); a malformed pending file aborts every map operation silently.","suggested_fix":"Use `\"${G}/a2a/\"*/decisions-pending.yaml`; default `$all` to `[]` when empty and guard the jq merge with `|| die`.","anchor_status":"valid","answered_by":"claude-headless"}

### DISS-C-012 [ADVISORY] voice=claude-headless
{"category":"error-handling","anchor":".claude/scripts/chart-frontier.sh:51","anchor_type":"line","anchor_line":51,"anchor_line_end":53,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"The frontier depends on `br ready --parent <epic> --type question --unassigned --limit 0 --json`, a flag combination only the PR's tests/fixtures/charting/br-stub.sh is known to accept. Any installed br that rejects one flag, or that treats `--limit 0` as 'zero results', yields either exit 1 with the misleading 'unknown epic?' message or a permanently empty frontier. `--root` affects only the map doc and the bv cwd; `br ready` runs in the caller's cwd, so the slug-to-epic resolution and the beads database can come from different trees.","failure_mode":"On a real br, /chart reports no tickets to work (or an unknown-epic error) for a map that has open question beads, and the session cannot progress.","suggested_fix":"Verify the flags against the pinned beads_rust version in install-br.sh and add a version check or a fallback to `br ready --json` with the parent/type/assignee filtering done in the existing jq FILTER; run br with `-C \"$ROOT\"` or `cd \"$ROOT\"`.","anchor_status":"valid","answered_by":"claude-headless"}

